    "https://www.hmc.edu/dean-of-faculty/2026/08/06/jenna-and-paul-segal-endowed-professorship-of-artificial-intelligence/": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Jenna and Paul Segal Endowed Professorship of Artificial Intelligence | Faculty Positions | Harvey Mudd College Skip to main content Skip to navigation for this section Home Resources for Resources for Students Faculty and Staff Alumni Parents Mudd A–Z Open search Admission and Financial Aid Toggle Admission dropdown menu Discover Harvey Mudd Connect to Harvey Mudd Apply to Harvey Mudd Afford to attend Harvey Mudd Academics Toggle Academics Dropdown DEPARTMENTS Biology Chemistry Computer Science Engineering Humanities, Social Sciences, and the Arts Mathematics Physics INTERDISCIPLINARY CENTERS Hixon Center for Climate and the Environment Center for Design Education Hixon-Riggs Program for Responsive Science and Engineering Majors at Harvey Mudd Academic Emphases at Harvey Mudd Faculty of Harvey Mudd Common Core Curriculum English Language Learning Student Awards and Fellowships Registrar Dean of the Faculty Institutional Research Learning Programs Study Abroad Upward Bound Summer Session The Makerspace Artificial Intelligence Innovation at Mudd Entrepreneurship Advanced STEAM Pre-collegiate Immersion for Research and Exploration (ASPIRE) Clinic Toggle Dropdown Sponsors and Projects Prospective Sponsors Impact on Society Clinic Events History of the Clinic Program Clinic Program Contacts Research Toggle Dropdown Summer Research and Scholarship Scholarship Focus Areas and Research Labs Research Videos Sponsored Faculty Research HMC-Sponsored Faculty Research Grants Postdoctoral Program in Interdisciplinary Computation Student Research Opportunities Student Life Toggle Dropdown Academic Resources and Study Abroad Campus Life Career Services Civic and Community Engagement Housing and Residential Life Institutional Diversity Wellbeing About Division of Student Affairs Meet the DSA Staff Dean of Students ASHMC Athletics Commencement Orientation Accessible Education International Students and Scholars Study Abroad Mudders Care for Mudders Emergency Resources Student Handbook Hazing Prevention and Policy Title IX and Sexual Assault Workplace Violence Policy 7C Demonstration Policy Annual Fire Safety and Security Report About Toggle Dropdown Visit Campus Harvey Mudd  News Upcoming Events Fast Facts History President's Office Mission and Strategic Planning Giving Toggle Dropdown Make Your Gift Now Annual Fund Endowed Giving at Harvey Mudd Planned Giving Current and Special Giving Initiatives Ways to Give Contact College Advancement Close Submit Faculty Positions Home Dean of the Faculty Faculty Positions Jenna and Paul Segal Endowed Professorship of Artificial Intelligence DOF Menu Dean of the Faculty Office of the Dean of the Faculty Academic Affairs Toggle sub-menu of Academic Affairs Exam Schedules Academic Affairs for Incoming Students Academic Affairs for Current Students Faculty Positions Faculty Development at Harvey Mudd College Toggle sub-menu of Faculty Development at Harvey Mudd College Faculty Development through NCFDD Faculty Policies and Procedures Faculty Mentoring Council of Undergraduate Research Resources for Early-Career Faculty Internal Items See Also Faculty Research Resources Honor Code Resources Innovation Accelerator (IA) Grants – Guidelines and Procedures webpage Jenna and Paul Segal Endowed Professorship of Artificial Intelligence August 6, 2026 Harvey Mudd College (HMC) invites applications for the inaugural Jenna and Paul Segal Endowed Professorship of Artificial Intelligence. The successful candidate will help build and advance the College’s human-centered, interdisciplinary vision for AI ( hmc.edu/ai ). They will join a collaborative faculty creatively exploring AI across the disciplines and through the College’s interdisciplinary centers. We seek an exemplary teacher-scholar who will explore the technical frontiers of AI intertwined with its human, ethical and societal implications, while preparing students to collaborate with AI systems in real-world contexts.  We anticipate hiring at the Assistant Professor level, but exceptional candidates at all ranks are encouraged to apply. We welcome applications from scholars of AI with connections to any discipline—including but not limited to the sciences, engineering, mathematics, humanities, social sciences, and the arts. The successful candidate will provide students with vibrant AI research experiences and develop innovative AI curricula, including courses and programming that support AI education, at HMC and beyond.  In addition to offering courses at the forefront of AI technological advances, the candidate will be expected to articulate how the ethical, societal, and human-centered dimensions of AI inform their research and teaching. Harvey Mudd College is a highly selective liberal arts college of science, engineering, and mathematics. It is located in Claremont, CA, approximately 35 miles east of Los Angeles, at the foot of the San Gabriel Mountains. Our residential, living-learning community of 900 students thrives on close student-faculty connections, requiring fully on campus teaching presence. We are looking for faculty who are eager to engage deeply with students both inside and outside the classroom. Our innovative and rigorous curriculum prepares students for both employment and graduate school and includes an active research program involving a substantial number of undergraduates.  Harvey Mudd College is a member of the Claremont Colleges, which comprises five undergraduate colleges (Pomona College, Scripps College, Claremont McKenna College, Harvey Mudd College, Pitzer College) and two postgraduate institutions (Claremont Graduate University and the Keck Graduate Institute).  Harvey Mudd College is committed to broadening participation in STEM fields. Among the criteria for appointment are demonstrated effectiveness in teaching and mentoring a broad range of students, including those from historically underserved backgrounds. Important Note: All registered classes taught during the academic year must be taught in person and on campus, in line with the HMC Academic Catalog and HMC Faculty Notebook. To streamline the initial application process, we invite candidates to submit a streamlined preliminary application packet consisting of only two items: Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter (3-4 pages) addressing the following: How an undergraduate liberal arts STEM environment aligns with your professional and scholarly goals. How you plan to engage undergraduate students in high-impact AI research and contribute to AI curricula across campus. Your vision for integrating the ethical, societal, or human-centered dimensions of AI into your work and teaching. How your teaching and mentorship will foster an inclusive environment for students from diverse backgrounds. A brief statement indicating which academic department(s) at HMC you feel would be most appropriate for your appointment, given your background and scholarly interests. The preliminary application packet should be submitted to AcademicJobsOnline: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32411 .  Note: Full dossier materials (e.g., complete research/teaching portfolios and recommendation letters) will only be requested from candidates invited to the long-list interview stage.  Questions should be sent to Dean of Faculty Karl Haushalter via email to AI_Professor_Search@g.hmc.edu. Successful candidates should have completed a Ph.D. in a relevant field by the time of appointment. The anticipated 9-month salary range for the assistant professor level is $115k – 135k, depending on experience.  In addition, Harvey Mudd is pleased to offer a robust benefits package, including faculty housing assistance and a dependent collegiate scholarship program. The search is currently open and will continue until the position is filled. Priority consideration will be given to candidates who submit their initial materials by September 22, 2026. Harvey Mudd College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Qualified applicants will be given consideration for employment without regard to age, race, gender, national origin, sexual orientation, protected veteran’s status, disability, or any other status protected by applicable law. https://www.hmc.edu/human-resources/policies-procedures-and-guidelines/equal-opportunity-and-nondiscrimination-statement/ Browse by Category Select category… Uncategorized Go Browse by Date Select month... August 2026 Go Employment Opportunity and Nondiscrimination Harvey Mudd College is an equal opportunity employer committed to providing a workplace free of discrimination, harassment, and disrespectful or other unprofessional conduct. Employment Opportunity and Nondiscrimination Statement . Request Info Visit Apply 301 Platt Blvd., Claremont, CA 91711 909.621.8000 | info@hmc.edu Your support helps educate compassionate leaders in STEM. Give now » The official store for Harvey Mudd College apparel and merchandise Shop HMC » Safety Information Immigration Resources & Information Mudders Care for Mudders Map and Directions Directory Privacy Statement Accessibility Equal Opportunity and Nondiscrimination Statement Employment at Harvey Mudd Harvey Mudd College does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of any status or condition protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. © Copyright 2026 | Harvey Mudd College is a member of The Claremont Colleges Harvey Mudd College Official Facebook Harvey Mudd College Official Instagram Harvey Mudd College Official BlueSky Harvey Mudd College Official YouTube Harvey Mudd College Official Flickr Harvey Mudd College Official LinkedIn"
    }
